WEBVTT

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.310
Good evening. Campaigners have been protesting against a third runway at Heathrow.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:24.910
They're unhappy about possible airport expansion and the effects it will have on climate change.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.970
Heathrow says the protest was carried out by a minority and its development plans...

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.050
would meet tough emissions targets.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.370
Here's our transport correspondent, Mike Pearce.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.090
A day of protest at Heathrow.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.150
At Terminal 2, they laid on the floor pretending they were dead.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.770
It's in protest at emissions they say will come with a third runway.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.170
Meanwhile, others took to their bikes in another protest.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.150
Any chance of disruption was never going to be possible

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.150
because of a massive police presence.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.870
Those here say the scheme is bad for the environment

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.490
and those under the flood path.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:05.270
If this airport gets expanded, not only will it be devastating for the local communities who will be displaced,

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.950
who will have to deal with the local noise and air pollution,

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:13.770
this will also mean catastrophic climate change for hundreds of thousands of people all over the world.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:17.570
We're constantly affected by night flights and flights all through the day.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.830
And when they talk about the fact that they're going to be increasing the flights,

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.310
the added pollution in the area is just too much.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:29.970
I've come from my children and my grandchildren, basically, because I want the world still to be an inhabitant.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.900
place for them and the way we're going it's not going to be inhabitable in not

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.890
very long time at all. The emissions that you know the next runway would bring is

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:45.340
just ridiculous I think we need to stand up and say no. Heathrow say the 17

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:50.600
billion pound scheme will create 70,000 local jobs and boost the economy. This

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.860
week they revealed plans for 25,000 more flights ahead of the new runway and

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.140
promised earlier environmental benefits. What we're proposing to do is to move

00:01:59.140 --> 00:01:59.960
from other

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.940
first plane coming at half past four to come in at half past five.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.780
We're also, people want more and more local jobs.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.920
And under these proposals, we are proposing to have up to 5,000 additional jobs

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.580
at the airport from 2021, which we will work with local authorities

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.020
to ensure that as many as possible of those jobs go to local people.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.080
But if the scheme goes ahead, protests like these will become a way of life.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.480
A decision is due towards the end of the month.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.880
Mike Pearce, ITV News, Heathrow.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.940
A man's undergone emergency surge.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.160
after being stabbed in broad daylight in Bournemouth.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.640
He was found with serious injuries on Regent Drive

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.080
in the Little Down area of the town yesterday afternoon.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.240
The man who's in his 20s was stabbed in the chest.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.220
Police are appealing for witnesses.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.850
Detectives searching for two men who abducted

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.470
and sexually assaulted a teenage girl in Oxford

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.750
have released descriptions of the offenders.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:58.770
The 14-year-old was forced into a silver hatchback car

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.970
on Wednesday morning on...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.360
Banbury Road in Summertown. One man is described as in his 20s, six feet tall with shaved dark

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:12.460
blonde hair. His belief to have a northern accent. The second has brown hair and is in his late teens

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:19.120
or early 20s. Police say the victim is being supported by specially trained officers. And

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.640
there is more on this story and the rest of the day's news in the Meridian region on our website

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.900
itv.com forward slash Meridian. Detectives will be speaking.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.260
to drivers and pedestrians tomorrow, a week after a serious assault on a 69-year-old man

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:41.080
in Gosport who later died. Roy Galvin hid his head on the road following a dispute with a

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:48.580
cyclist. He died three days later. A man's been charged with manslaughter. Concern is growing

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:54.100
for a teenager from Sussex who's gone missing. 16-year-old Bonnie Clark was last seen at 11

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:59.960
o'clock on Monday night. Detectives believe she may be in the Brighton area. She's described as

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.700
white, about five feet ten, with shoulder-length blonde hair. She wears glasses and has a Welsh

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:11.200
accent. Anyone who has seen her or knows where she is, is asked to contact Sussex Police.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:18.810
A company in Sussex that makes dairy products has been fined £8,000 for polluting the River

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:24.510
Curd in Billingshurst. Crouchlands Farms Limited allowed dirty water and diluted slurry to

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:29.710
contaminate the water over an eight-mile stretch. Fish and river life were affected.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:36.150
On to football now, and it was a busy day for the teams here in the Meridian region.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:40.290
In the Premier League, Bournemouth drew 2-0 with Watford.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.910
In the Championship, Reading were at home to Derby and drew 1-0.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.990
And Brighton beat Sheffield Wednesday 2-1.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.590
In League One, Oxford United face Bolton.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.710
Final score there, Bolton 0, Oxford United 2.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.710
While Swindon drew 1-0 against Shrewsbury.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.800
And in League 2,

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.660
Crawley beat Blackpool 1-0.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.360
And Portsmouth at home to Doncaster lost.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.800
Score there, Doncaster 2, Portsmouth 1.

